  "releaseNotes": "v4.0.0 — two removals, both flagged in v3. Nothing new is added and no runtime behaviour changes.\n\nBreaking: EntityId<TValue>'s conversion to its underlying value is now explicit. While it was\nimplicit, a strongly-typed id was accepted anywhere its underlying type was expected, so any two id\ntypes over the same primitive were mutually substitutable — exactly what strongly-typed ids exist to\nprevent. Use .Value, or cast.\n\nBreaking: IAggregateRoot.DomainEvents and ClearDomainEvents() are removed. Both were [Obsolete] in\n3.0.0; use GetUncommittedEvents() and MarkChangesAsCommitted().\n\nFull upgrade guide with diffs: see \"Upgrading to v4.0\" in the README.",
